+Relations carry the type their author wrote (`- depends_on [[Target]]`), and a
+wiki link in prose is an implicit `links_to`. By default every edge is followed
+and all of them compete for the same `max_related` budget. `relation_types`
+follows only the listed types, `exclude_relation_types` skips them (pass
+`["links_to"]` to keep just the explicitly typed relations), and `direction`
+picks the side of the edge: `outgoing` is what the note declares, `incoming`
+is what points at it. Each filter applies at every hop, so
+`relation_types=["depends_on"]` with `depth=2` returns transitive dependencies
+and nothing else. Type labels match exactly as written in the note.
+
